{"tool_name":"livecell","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"livecell","home":"https://github.com/sartorius-research/LIVECell","license":"MIT","summary":"A large-scale dataset for label-free live cell segmentation","addition_date":"2022-02-20T16:44:17.495841Z","last_update_date":"2022-02-20T16:44:17.498406Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:livecell","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"Rickard.Sjoegren@Sartorius.com","name":"Rickard Sj\u00f6gren","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7881-0968","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Nabeel Khalid"},{"name":"Nicola Bevan"},{"name":"Christoffer Edlund","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0003-3681"},{"name":"Timothy R. Jackson","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8539-455X"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://sartorius-research.github.io/LIVECell/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"},{"term":"Image annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3553"},{"term":"Parsing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_1812"},{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"}]}],"name":"LIVECell","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/S41592-021-01249-6","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Light microscopy combined with well-established protocols of two-dimensional cell culture facilitates high-throughput quantitative imaging to study biological phenomena. Accurate segmentation of individual cells in images enables exploration of complex biological questions, but can require sophisticated imaging processing pipelines in cases of low contrast and high object density. Deep learning-based methods are considered state-of-the-art for image segmentation but typically require vast amounts of annotated data, for which there is no suitable resource available in the field of label-free cellular imaging. Here, we present LIVECell, a large, high-quality, manually annotated and expert-validated dataset of phase-contrast images, consisting of over 1.6 million cells from a diverse set of cell morphologies and culture densities. To further demonstrate its use, we train convolutional neural network-based models using LIVECell and evaluate model segmentation accuracy with a proposed a suite of benchmarks.","authors":[{"name":"Ahmed S."},{"name":"Bevan N."},{"name":"Dale T."},{"name":"Dengel A."},{"name":"Edlund C."},{"name":"Jackson T.R."},{"name":"Khalid N."},{"name":"Sjogren R."},{"name":"Trygg J."}],"citationCount":2,"date":"2021-09-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"LIVECell\u2014A large-scale dataset for label-free live cell segmentation"},"pmcid":"PMC8440198","pmid":"34462594"}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Protein expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0108"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"LIVECell","home":"https://bio.tools/livecell","license":"MIT","summary":"A large-scale dataset for label-free live cell segmentation","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:livecell/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"buil